        <item>
            <title>0.3.9</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 21 Apr 2026 02:10:35 -0400</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1776751628</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.3.9</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
  body { font-family: -apple-system, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; padding: 12px; }
  h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 14px; }
  h2 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 12px; }
  ul { margin: 4px 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  li { margin: 2px 0; }
</style>
<h3>What's New</h3>
<h2>New Features</h2>
<ul>
<li>Added a Populate button to the Why card that appears on hover, kicking off a guided interview to fill in your project philosophy.</li>
<li>Code review submissions now support chunked/progressive review for large diffs, letting you review big PRs in manageable passes.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Improvements</h2>
<ul>
<li>Chat now uses a virtualized list, so conversations with hundreds of messages scroll, resize, and stream updates dramatically faster without UI stalls.</li>
<li>Context window sizes updated for the latest models: Claude Opus 4.7/4.6 and Sonnet 4.6 now use a 1M window, GPT-5 Codex variants use 400K, and Gemini 3 Pro/Flash are recognized. Addy also prefers its own known limits when a CLI reports a stale smaller value, so the gauge reflects the model&#x27;s real capacity.</li>
<li>The review pane got a visual refresh: cancel button, pill-style severity badges, meta cards with commit and file info, and a cleaner dropdown for switching between reviews.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Attachment carousel polish</h2>
<ul>
<li>more prominent navigation arrows, a full-width bottom border, and gradients that now sit flush to the edges.</li>
<li>The conversation sidebar preview and chat resizing no longer stutter on the main thread, making window resizing and session switching feel noticeably snappier.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Bug Fixes</h2>
<ul>
<li>Fixed a reentrant crash in the chat list that could occur while messages streamed in during a layout pass.</li>
<li>Resolved Auto Layout conflicts that could log warnings or cause jitter in the pane header bar, memory view, and expandable cards on hover.</li>
<li>Fixed several chat display issues including scroll anchoring, diff rendering, and text-content link handling regressions.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Internal Changes</h2>
<ul>
<li>Added a native frame-pointer backtrace sampler (AddyBacktrace) used to pinpoint main-thread stalls, enabling the performance work above.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
